      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update gradle-9 to 9.7.1-r1 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-71497 (GHSA-pmhh-3w7g-xqp8): the jsoup Cleaner can let markup through when a custom Safelist permits raw-text elements; the built-in Safelists are not affected. jsoup 1.14.3 to 1.22.2 is affected and 1.23.1 fixes it (https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/security/advisories/GHSA-pmhh-3w7g-xqp8, fix commit https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/commit/92f1aca552548b484bc7d4b94c51e48b8e6eca70). We read every gradle-9 package published for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository as of 2026-11-27: 22 versions, 9.4.0-r0 to 9.9.2-r0. Each aarch64 package has the same index checksum as the x86_64 package of that version (9.6.1-r3 and 9.6.1-r4 are published for x86_64 only), so we read the x86_64 packages, checked each against its index checksum, and read every jar in them, including nested jars, taking each library version from the Maven metadata inside the jar under /usr/share/java/gradle/lib, not from the file name. jsoup is 1.15.3 in 9.4.0-r0 to 9.6.1-r6, 1.22.2 in 9.7.0-r1 and 9.7.1-r0 and 1.23.1 in 9.7.1-r1, each byte for byte the Maven Central release of its version, and no build from 9.8.0-r1 to 9.9.2-r0 holds jsoup classes in any jar, relocated or not (the same scan finds the jackson classes in those builds). No other jar in any build holds jsoup classes. Every build before 9.7.1-r1 carries an affected jsoup and no later build carries an affected one, so the range ends at 9.7.1-r1."
    },
